format 1
adapter characters 1

npc npc-hal
name: Hal
title: Atom teacher
field: atoms

bio:
    I am Hal. I teach what is inside the atom, slowly and exactly, because small things deserve it. I keep rocks on my desk and I have named every one. Reginald is in charge.

spec:
    {
      "skin": {
        "base": "#FFCBA3",
        "shade": "#F5B585",
        "feature": "#E99B5F"
      },
      "head": "capsule",
      "headWidth": 106,
      "eyes": "pill",
      "nose": "button",
      "hair": {
        "style": "cloud",
        "color": "#FFB100",
        "shade": "#E7A601"
      },
      "outfit": {
        "kind": "whitecoat",
        "color": "#2B70C9",
        "shade": "#1453A3",
        "collar": "#D2E4E8"
      },
      "accent": {
        "kind": "sample",
        "color": "#E5A259",
        "shade": "#A56644"
      },
      "cover": {
        "color": "#FFC800",
        "shade": "#E7A601"
      }
    }

line line-hal-meet
kind: meet
pose: greet

    Hi, I'm Hal. Let's find out what everything is made of.

line line-hal-sign-off
kind: sign_off
pose: proud

    Well done. Now you know what is inside an atom, and why that matters.

line line-hal-tease
kind: tease
pose: idle

    Finish my unit first, and I'll show you the rest.

line line-hal-intro-atoms-are-everywhere
kind: lesson_intro
pose: greet
lesson: atoms-are-everywhere

    Today you'll see what everything around you is made of, and how small an atom really is.

line line-hal-intro-elements-and-the-periodic-table
kind: lesson_intro
pose: point
lesson: elements-and-the-periodic-table

    The number of protons tells you which element an atom is. Let's build some.

line line-hal-intro-isotopes
kind: lesson_intro
pose: explain
lesson: isotopes

    Atoms of one element can differ a little. You'll learn what isotopes are.

line line-hal-intro-protons-neutrons-electrons
kind: lesson_intro
pose: explain
lesson: protons-neutrons-electrons

    We'll open up an atom and meet its three particles. You'll learn what each one does.

line line-hal-intro-stable-and-unstable-nuclei
kind: lesson_intro
pose: think
lesson: stable-and-unstable-nuclei

    Some nuclei stay the same and some can change. You'll see why that matters.
